        <groundspeak:log id="619435490">
          <groundspeak:date>2016-07-12T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="946600">Black Shark</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP579 Lily Lake Road&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;From the road we could see two beribboned lathes.  The flagging tape looked pretty fresh and bright and we hoped that this cap would not pose the problems that it has to some other finders.  Sure enough, it had been dug out recently (thank you WillowZilla) and there was only a layer of dirt washed in by recent rains.  The little shovel made quick work of it and the brush finished it off.  The cap is now bordered on two sides by a vibrant canola field.  Quite lovely.  Thanks, outforthehunt, for the 19 caps that enhanced our SRT mega weekend!  They exposed us to new types of markers, brought us to interesting places and gave us memories that will bring us joy for a long, long time.  Thanks, too, to those who maintain the supporting pages for this cache.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="617512408">
          <groundspeak:log_wpt lat="53.841333" lon="-113.401533" />
          <groundspeak:date>2016-07-10T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="11091667">WillowZilla</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP579 - Lily Lake Road&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Heading home from Cold Lake after the SRT mega I figured I'd hit as many caps as i could on the way home. Oh kind of disappointing that the field has used this location as a dumping ground for mulch and leftover dirt from the nearby track.  Luckily for me, someone had put some lath and flagging tape in, so i dug between them, with my hands only, but everything was wet and soft, so only about a foot down I uncovered the cap. :)&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="537535113">
          <groundspeak:date>2015-07-25T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Didn't find it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="1780878">k5&#162;ents</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP579 Lily Lake Road&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I'm sure the cap is in there somewhere, but I had to give this one a pass.

Next time I'll come prepared with big shovels to move all the mulch.

Thanks.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
      </groundspeak:logs>
